---
import "./work.css";
import { homeContactHrefFromPagePath } from "../../../lib/leadSource";
import { CTA_PRIMARY_CONTACT } from "../../../site/cta";

const DEMO_URL = "https://barberdemo.kersivo.co.uk/";
const pagePath = Astro.url.pathname.replace(/\/+$/, "") || "/";
const homeContactHref = homeContactHrefFromPagePath(pagePath);
---

<article class="cs-page section" aria-labelledby="cs-barber-title">
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="cs-back" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol class="cs-back__list">
        <li>
          <a href="/work/">Selected work</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cs-back__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <span class="cs-back__here">Barber website system</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <header class="cs-header">
      <div class="cs-header__eyebrow">
        <span class="k-kicker k-kicker--md">Studio product · live demo</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="cs-title" id="cs-barber-title">Barber website system</h1>
      <p class="cs-client-line">
        A live demonstration for UK barbershops &mdash; bookings, retail, and admin in one build
      </p>

      <div class="cs-tags" aria-label="Project type and focus">
        <span class="cs-tag">2025–26</span>
        <span class="cs-tag">Product system</span>
        <span class="cs-tag">Bookings UX</span>
        <span class="cs-tag">E-commerce</span>
        <a
          class="cs-tag cs-tag--url"
          href={DEMO_URL}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer noopener"
          aria-label="Open barber system live demo in new tab"
        >
          barberdemo.kersivo.co.uk <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="cs-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="cs-intro">
      <div class="cs-intro__body">
        <p>
          This is not a bespoke one-to-one client commission. It is a branded, live demonstration
          of a <strong>productised website system</strong> for barbershops: the same UX discipline
          and engineering quality we apply to custom work, packaged for a specific vertical.
        </p>
        <p>
          The demo exists so owners can see a complete, operational surface &mdash; booking flow,
          shop and pickup, pricing, FAQs, and admin-led updates &mdash; without relying on a generic
          template or a patchwork of third-party tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="cs-scope" aria-label="What this demonstration includes">
        <h2 class="cs-scope__heading">What it demonstrates</h2>
        <ul class="cs-scope__list" role="list">
          <li>Vertical-specific IA and conversion narrative</li>
          <li>Integrated booking journey (UX and UI)</li>
          <li>Retail &amp; pickup commerce experience</li>
          <li>Barber schedules, services, and catalogue structure</li>
          <li>Operational admin workflows (content, products, day-to-day)</li>
          <li>Premium presentation &amp; performance-led front-end</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-challenge">
      <span class="cs-section-label" aria-hidden="true">Why it exists</span>
      <blockquote class="cs-challenge__pull">
        <p>
          Barbershops often run on disconnected tools. The website should feel like one
          sharp brand &mdash; not a brochure that hands off to five other tabs.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="cs-challenge__body">
        Many shops juggle separate booking widgets, social proof scattered across platforms, and
        retail that never quite connects to how clients actually book. The demo shows how a single,
        calm system can carry the full story: from first visit to booked appointment or product
        pickup, with less daily friction for the team.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-preview-wrap">
      <figure class="cs-browser" aria-label="Barber website system demo preview">
        <div class="cs-browser__bar" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="cs-browser__dots">
            <span class="cs-dot cs-dot--red"></span>
            <span class="cs-dot cs-dot--yellow"></span>
            <span class="cs-dot cs-dot--green"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-browser__address">barberdemo.kersivo.co.uk</div>
          <div class="cs-browser__spacer"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-browser__viewport">
          <img
            class="cs-browser__img"
            src="/screenshots/barber-system-desktop.jpg"
            alt="Kersivo barber system demo — homepage showing booking and retail messaging"
            width="1200"
            height="760"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />

          <div class="cs-browser__fallback" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="cs-browser__fallback-inner">
              <span class="cs-browser__fallback-url">barberdemo.kersivo.co.uk</span>
              <span class="cs-browser__fallback-hint">Barber website system &mdash; live demo</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="cs-browser__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>

          <a
            class="cs-browser__live"
            href={DEMO_URL}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer noopener"
            aria-label="Open barber system live demo in new tab"
          >
            View live demo <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <figcaption class="cs-browser__caption">
          Demonstration environment &mdash; homepage, desktop view
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-built">
      <header class="cs-built__header">
        <span class="cs-section-label">Inside the system</span>
        <h2 class="cs-built__title">
          Built to book.<br />Built to sell.<br />Built to run the shop.
        </h2>
      </header>

      <div class="cs-built__grid">
        <div class="cs-built__card">
          <h3>Connected booking journey</h3>
          <p>
            Self-serve booking is part of the same brand experience as the rest of the site &mdash;
            not an iframe that breaks trust or adds platform clutter.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-built__card">
          <h3>Retail and pickup</h3>
          <p>
            Product merchandising, cart, and pickup logic are designed to sit alongside services,
            so clients can browse and buy without leaving the barbershop&apos;s own property.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-built__card">
          <h3>Operational clarity</h3>
          <p>
            Services, team, schedules, and day-to-day updates are structured for teams that need
            speed &mdash; fewer workarounds, clearer ownership of content.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-built__card">
          <h3>Sales-led homepage</h3>
          <p>
            The narrative is intentional: proof, process, packages, and objections handled in one
            flow &mdash; similar to how we structure high-converting bespoke builds.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-built__card">
          <h3>Premium craft in the details</h3>
          <p>
            Typography, motion restraint, and layout rhythm match a high-end studio standard. The
            demo is meant to feel like a real shop &mdash; not a stock theme.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-built__card">
          <h3>Performance as a feature</h3>
          <p>
            Lean architecture and fast delivery matter for local search and on-the-go clients.
            The front-end is built with the same performance discipline as client launches.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-outcomes">
      <span class="cs-section-label">What this proves</span>
      <h2 class="cs-outcomes__title">Product depth without cutting corners.</h2>

      <ul class="cs-outcomes__list" role="list">
        <li class="cs-outcome">
          <span class="cs-outcome__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <p>
            We can ship a <strong>complete vertical system</strong> &mdash; not only marketing
            pages &mdash; when the business model calls for bookings and commerce together.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="cs-outcome">
          <span class="cs-outcome__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <p>
            The demo is intentionally <strong>live and explorable</strong>, so you can judge
            interaction quality, pacing, and clarity the same way you would a client site.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="cs-outcome">
          <span class="cs-outcome__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <p>
            Positioning stays honest: this entry is labeled as a studio product, distinct from
            bespoke engagements like Sewing Ataga &mdash; transparency builds trust.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="cs-outcome">
          <span class="cs-outcome__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <p>
            If you run a barbershop and want this system for your brand, pricing and onboarding are
            outlined on the demo. For fully custom briefs outside this vertical, start with a
            conversation on the main site.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-cta" role="region" aria-label="Next steps with Kersivo">
      <div class="cs-cta__inner">
        <p class="cs-cta__pre">Interested?</p>
        <h2 class="cs-cta__title">
          Custom build, or a proven system for your vertical.
        </h2>
        <p class="cs-cta__body">
          If you are exploring the barber system, use the live demo to review packages and book a
          walkthrough. For other UK businesses, tell us about your brief &mdash; we will advise on
          the right route (bespoke build, productised setup, or hybrid).
        </p>
        <div class="cs-cta__actions">
          <a
            href={homeContactHref}
            class="k-btn k-btn--primary k-btn--magnetic"
            data-magnetic="true"
            data-cta="contact"
          >
            <span class="k-btn__label">{CTA_PRIMARY_CONTACT}</span>
            <span class="k-btn__shine" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="k-btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
          </a>
          <a href={DEMO_URL} class="k-btn k-btn--ghost" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">
            <span class="k-btn__label">Open live demo</span>
            <span class="k-btn__arrow2" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
